WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.490
Pretty freaking powerful?

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:03.530
Yes, I agree.

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:10.790
Hey guys its Max from Max Tech, Its been almost
two years since Apple refreshed the iMac lineup.

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:15.560
We love our 2017 5K, but as the time went
on and Intel released new processor after

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.520
processor we started feeling like this was
the next trashcan Mac pro.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.640
Thankfully, Apple didn’t disappoint and
we now have a 9th gen 8 core i9 available

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.840
that is rated up to 5Ghz.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:31.160
Yes, this thing should beat he $5000 iMac
Pro is basically every task.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.500
And Yes, we do have one ordered.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.469
We’ll be doing direct comparisons and other
tests like benchmarks and gaming with the

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:40.519
new Vega 48 graphics so make sure to subscribe
and enable those notifications.

00:00:40.519 --> 00:00:44.309
Now I do have a few serious concerns, but
before I talk about them and dig deeper on

00:00:44.309 --> 00:00:46.629
the i9 model, I want to touch on the 21.

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:51.179
It used to be a good device for normal use
but with the addition of 6 core CPU’s and

00:00:51.179 --> 00:00:54.760
new graphics, this will be the first time
I’ll be recommending the smaller iMac for

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:55.929
video editing.

00:00:55.929 --> 00:01:00.489
For $1499 you get a sharp, bright, and color
accurate 4K display with the same graphics

00:01:00.489 --> 00:01:05.360
that's in the $2800 Macbook Pro and a CPU
that’s practically as fast.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.850
This does, of course, come with a Fusion drive
and 8GB of RAM, so I would suggest upgrading

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:14.270
to the base SSD for $100 more and if you can
16GB of RAM.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:18.240
Have a bit more cash then spring for Vega
20 graphics and you’ll have a powerful iMac

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.950
rivaling my high-end MacBook that costs $1000
more.

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:23.250
Photo editing instead of video?

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:28.680
Skip the graphics upgrade go for 32GB of RAM
instead for a photoshop and lightroom powerhouse.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:32.049
As always we’ll leave links in the description
for the models we recommend along with ram

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:33.049
which I’ll mention in just a bit.

00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:34.049
Now onto the 5K.

00:01:34.049 --> 00:01:37.640
Unfortunately, we didn't get a redesign with
slimmer bezels like we wanted but a benefit

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:42.140
of that is still having access to the RAM
slots which will save you some serious cash.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:45.929
The base graphics have an X attached to them
meaning they are slightly faster than the

00:01:45.929 --> 00:01:46.929
previous versions.

00:01:46.929 --> 00:01:51.530
We have 6 cores across the board but the best
bang for the buck is the top $2299 tier since

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:56.030
its the only one getting a 9th gen CPU and
comes standard with 580X graphics.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:59.810
Like always I’d spend the $100 to jump to
the SSD.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:05.710
Apple charges a whopping $600 for an additional
24GB of RAM but we’re going to save some

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:10.229
cash and buy our own 32GB kit for only $180.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:14.890
It easy only takes a few mins to install and
doesn’t void your warranty, In fact, Apple

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:17.300
even has a how-to guide on their website.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:24.120
We end up saving $420 and as a bonus, we have
40GB of RAM instead of 32, which is enough

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.500
for most high-end users.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:30.220
I’ll leave a link to the RAM I bought down
below.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:31.430
So is this impressive?

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:32.760
I’d say definitely!

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:37.810
For $300 less than yesterday, we have an iMac
with faster RAM, Graphics, and Processor.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:42.510
Apple has been charging more where they can,
so it's nice to see a cheaper Mac fast enough

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.570
for most 4K video editors.

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:47.070
So what about that iMac Pro Killer?

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:50.340
Like I mentioned Apple has been raising the
average sales price on its products and if

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:55.650
you opt for the newly offered i9 and Vega
graphics you’ll spend $550 more than the

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.670
previous top-spec 5K iMac.

00:02:57.670 --> 00:03:00.210
But do I care, no not really!

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:03.900
Most people who buy this configuration can
afford it, and the price increase isn't for

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:07.840
an average performance bump but one that should
perform better than an iMac Pro.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:09.850
[Show: professionals, business owners, People
who have a lot of money]

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:10.850
How?

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:14.230
Well, our 2017 iMac already performed better
in some tasks, but where it really struggled

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:18.340
is heavy tasks like RAW video editing because
it was limited to 4 cores.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:22.811
We now have an 8 core option but with faster
clock speeds meaning that not only will it

00:03:22.811 --> 00:03:27.590
have extra grunt when you're maxing out your
CPU but also for most tasks where you typically

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:29.670
don’t pin your processor to 100%.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:36.090
The 9th gen architecture is also more efficient
so it also faster per clock than the Xeon.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:40.730
Onto the graphics, we have a Vega 48 option
but honestly, I’m not sure how much faster

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:46.620
it is compared to the 580X or Vega 56 in the
iMac pro, but we will find out soon in our

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.340
full performance comparison videos.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:53.250
I am fairly optimistic though since its a
much newer chip than the Vega 56 and because

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:58.340
the Vega 20 in my MacBook made a big difference
in performance and also improved temps.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:01.840
This brings me to my first serious concern,
overheating.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:06.610
Previous 4 core iMacs already throttled so
hopefully, we don’t have the same issue

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.570
as with the i9 MacBooks.

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:12.790
This alone may be a good reason to go for
the cooler running vega graphics.

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:14.640
Next is no 10GBe.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:19.390
This isn’t a dealbreaker but since they
offer it in the iMac Pro and the new Mac Mini

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:23.650
I was hoping it would be available for fast
access to servers without adapters.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:26.770
Finally, Apple didn’t include the t2 chip.

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:31.270
This is odd since it has a lot of benefits
and is included in all of their new devices.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:35.910
I can only guess that they wanted to keep
this refresh as simple as possible since we

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:37.100
have the same exact IO.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:41.000
Overall we’re happy with the updates as
we really weren’t expecting an 8 core in

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.690
the regular iMac or Vega graphics.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:46.760
If you don’t need the very best you can
now get great performance for less money than

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:50.560
before, and even good 4K editing with the
21” iMac.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.910
As a reminder, we do have links to everything
in the description, and go ahead and click

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:59.530
here if you want to see how this thing performs
compared to the 2017 iMac and the iMac Pro.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:05.620
This has been Max with Mac tech and I’ll
see you in the next video.

